<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Interleisure first half boosted by excepts.</title>
<headline>Interleisure first half boosted by excepts.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-exceps (cts)  15.1	 vs 13.0</p>
<p>    Shr, post-exceps (cts) 25.5	 vs 12.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  6.75	 vs 6.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    48.44	vs 23.51</p>
<p>    Exceptional gain	 19.81	vs 1.07 charge</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    60.38	vs 35.51</p>
<p>    Tax			  11.97	vs 11.80</p>
<p>    Interest received	0.90	 vs 0.81 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		   250.37     vs 226.75</p>
<p>Div payable March 17</p>
<p>on register February 21</p>
<p>Full name: Interleisure Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The exceptional gain reflects profits on disposals. The company said cinema chain Ster-Kinekor was expected to enhance second half trading, although a marginal decline in activity in other areas could temper this slightly. Earnings growth for the full year is expected to be similar to that achieved in the first half.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
